      "type": "core.input.comment",
      "name": "comment",
      "x": 45,
      "y": 23.1,
      "text": "The order4 module passes any incoming message out all 4 outputs in order from bottom up.  This order can matter when using kickable and non-kickable jacks.\n\nToDo: Click the \"kick\" button on the counter module several times.\n\nNote that out3 sends before out4. So the B jack is set before the A jack is kicked. So the subtraction result is zero.\n\nNote that out1 sends to A before out2 sends to B. So the subtraction occurs before B is set. It just uses the previous value.",
